Professional Skills group presentation | Time Management & Productivity

My section lasts about two minutes. I planned one slide for the cost of procrastination and one for practical ways to get started.

Slide 5 - The Cost of Procrastination (about 45 seconds)

I selected the main findings from Tice and Baumeister (1997) for the slide.
The students who procrastinated reported more stress and illness towards the end of the semester and received lower grades.
I use the example of a group presentation left until the night before to explain what the delay can look like in practice.
A late start leaves the group less time to check sources, improve the slides and rehearse.

Slide 6 - Two Tools for Getting Started (about 75 seconds)

I carried the presentation example into this slide.
Writing a slide title illustrates the Two-Minute Rule, and drafting its main points illustrates a Pomodoro.
I put the 25-minute focus period and five-minute break in large type so the audience can see the timing while I explain the example.
I put the full script in the speaker notes.

Rehearsal plan

Run through both slides with a timer. Check that the research example and both techniques fit within two minutes.
End with a handoff to the next speaker, who will explain if-then plans.
